// /step N runs exactly N cycles and leaves the run paused.
//
// The point is that SEVERAL VALUES CAN BELONG TO ONE CYCLE. A `> X = 1' typed at
// the prompt runs a cycle of its own -- right for a person poking at one thing,
// wrong for a tool with three inputs for the same instant, which would get three
// cycles. /pause, set them all, /step is the sequence that behaves like hardware:
// every DIN committed at the top of one cycle.

#digital Led out 8
#variable V = 0
#states Home

#in INIT
    State = Home
#end

#in Home
    Led = 1 ? V
#end
